# Everything marimo needs, installed into the workspace image (/opt/marimo) so it works with no network at all:
# marimo with its optional features, and the libraries notebooks commonly import. To add a package, list it here,
# run ../../tools/build-workspace-image.sh (it pins every version into requirements.lock) and ship the new image.

# marimo and its extras: SQL cells (duckdb, polars, sqlglot), charts (altair), formatting (ruff), Jupyter import
# (nbformat), sandbox/uv, the AI assistant's client, and the language server (python-lsp-server, python-lsp-ruff).
marimo[recommended,lsp]==0.24.2

# Data and computation
numpy
pandas
pyarrow
scipy
scikit-learn
statsmodels
sympy
networkx

# Plotting and widgets (altair comes with marimo[recommended])
matplotlib
seaborn
plotly
vegafusion
vl-convert-python
anywidget

# Files and data sources
openpyxl
xlsxwriter
pillow
lxml
beautifulsoup4
requests
httpx
sqlalchemy
tabulate
jinja2
